commit 1cd4db44f41cf4dd70f4d6b02372861cb761a31e
Author: Karen Pendergrass <karen@paleofoundation.com>
Date:   Wed Jun 3 00:52:31 2026 +0300

    ingest: sacchi2021-balangero-asbestos-mine-groundwater fresh from Manual Fetch Kimi /June 2 Manual Fetches
    
    - Added Sacchi et al. 2021 (Water 13:735, DOI 10.3390/w13050735) natural background level
      characterisation of Cr, Cr-VI, Co, Ni, Mn, Fe, Zn in groundwater from the former Balangero
      chrysotile asbestos mine in serpentinite (Lanzo Massif, Piedmont, North Italy).
    - 29 monitoring stations across four hydrogeological formations (Sesia-Lanzo, Lanzo serpentinite,
      fluvioglacial deposits, Balangero Plain alluvium); 39-74 PTE measurements pooled across
      2012-2019 campaigns with complete 2019 hydrogeochemical characterisation.
    - Proposed NBLs: Cr 39.3, Cr-VI 38.1, Ni 84, Mn 71.36 (95p); Fe 58.4, Zn 232.2 (90p) µg/L.
      Cr-VI NBL flagged as not representative of the Balangero Plain alluvial aquifer.
    - Environmental natural-background characterisation; products/ingredients intentionally empty.
    - Direction check (Part 2): wiki-toward-literature; reports what the source measured at the
      Italian regulatory baseline without softening or strengthening for HMTc convenience.
    
    Routing: 0 product-page rows (non-food environmental source; advisory entry in routing_malformed.csv
    per established posture for sediment/groundwater/remediation sources).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

